' ── DECIDED 2026-11-14 (the owner) ─────────────────────────────────────────
'   S1 DIRECTION: sbx's model. One named sandbox per (harness, workspace),
'      kept and re-attached. History on a live host directory per (harness,
'      workspace). Delete the per-file state sync, volume@1 and the
'      retained-engine special case: OpenCode's retained engine and hermes's
'      live bind become the rule. The owner: "Note the hermes and opencode
'      exceptions in _plans/ to look for standardization" (THE TWO EXCEPTIONS
'      below).
'   S2 claude's sessions/ is VM-local: never carried between VMs. daemon.lock,
'      daemon/ and jobs/ likewise.
'   S3 Stop the volume leak in the stopgap. Drop the five volume@1 from the
'      vendored claude kit; upstream sbx/claude dropped them in 2.1.317. Carry
'      projects/<workspace keys> and todos/ through the stopgap's scoped
'      newer-wins copy. The stranded volumes (1,710 records) and the host's
'      ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions stay untouched, for the owner. [Inference]
'      The stranded volumes allocate about 91 GiB.
'
' ── RECONCILED: clone-workspace.puml "A CLONE LIVES FOR ONE RUN" ───────────
' Earlier the same day the owner accepted per-run clones: "as long as the end
' user perceives them as one and the same (session logs remain, etc) it does
' the expected job." That section (commit 3a86212b) names the stopgap's copy
' as the carrier and lists a durable clone as NOT CHOSEN. The sbx-intent
' research then showed that sbx means sandboxes to be kept and re-attached,
' and the owner chose that model (S1). The goal stands: the operator sees one
' session. The mechanism moves: the sandbox and its clone outlive the run (P1),
' and the history lives on the host (P2). That section stays current-state
' truth until P1 ships, and is rewritten then. Its NOT CHOSEN reasons become
' this plan's work:
'   a clone gone stale under a moving host checkout ...... P3
'   two concurrent runs on one key ........................ Q1
'   state with no lifecycle under `proveo clean` .......... Q2
' state-sync.puml calls this plan "a separate plan" and carries S2 itself:
' todos/ keeps the whole-store scope, and sessions/ no longer travels.
'
' ── WHAT sbx INTENDS (read 2026-11-14) ─────────────────────────────────────
' LIFECYCLE: long-lived, named, re-attached.
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/usage/ : "Sandboxes persist after the
'     agent exits." "Running the same workspace path again reconnects to the
'     existing sandbox rather than creating another sandbox".
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/architecture/ : "Sandboxes persist
'     until explicitly removed."
'   `sbx run --help` (v0.50.0): "To re-attach to an existing sandbox by name,
'     use --name". `sbx stop --help`: "Stopped sandboxes retain their state".
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/workflows/git/ : in clone mode,
'     "Dispatch each independent task to a separate background session", and
'     "A single clone-mode sandbox can hold multiple branches and worktrees
'     for parallel tasks." Its "keep one sandbox per project and reuse it
'     across tasks" sits under the mountless-sandbox section, not clone mode.
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/agents/claude-code/ : the parallel
'     form is `sbx run --clone claude . -- agents`, many sessions in one VM.
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/workflows/automation/ : disposable
'     sandboxes (`sbx create --name ci-task …`, `sbx rm --force`) are the CI
'     pattern, not the interactive one.
'   https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/775, a Docker member: "You
'     can run agents in parallel within the same sandbox, any reason to not do
'     it…?"
' STORAGE: live, found again by identity; never one archive.
'   https://github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec/blob/main/docs/spec/capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/volume@1.md
'     "Deleting a sandbox MUST NOT delete its block-volume storage by default".
'   https://github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec/issues/207, fixed by d50ad9f5
'     (2026-11-06): "The point of `volume@1` is that a sandbox that is deleted
'     and created again gets its own data back." The spec now says a runtime
'     "MUST let the operator list retained block storage" and "MUST NOT
'     silently expire" it.
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/author/patterns/ : sbx
'     "reattaches a volume when the sandbox name, kit source, and volume path
'     match"; "for local sources, the source directory must stay the same".
'   https://github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec/blob/main/docs/spec/capabilities/com.docker.sandbox/host-mount@1.md
'     "MUST keep the directory's contents independently of any sandbox";
'     "MUST key the directory on the declaring Kit's identity and the cleaned
'     `path`"; "the grant promises no locking". `sbx create --mount HOST:PATH`
'     (v0.50.0) binds a host directory to a declared host-mount@1 path, at
'     create only.
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/use-kits/ : "A different
'     sandbox name or kit source gets separate storage".
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/author/capabilities/ :
'     agent-sessions@1 only declares commands; "Docker Sandboxes does not
'     execute the declared session commands."
'   The only one-archive models: cloud volumes, where "the last sandbox to
'     exit overwrites the stored snapshot"
'     (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/cloud/usage/), and `sbx template
'     save` / `sbx move`, whole-filesystem images that leave mounted storage
'     out.
' PUBLISHED KITS (registry descriptors, 2026-11-14):
'   sbx/claude 2.1.267 declared five volume@1: projects 2g; sessions, todos,
'     shell-snapshots and statsig 512m each. 2.1.317 (2026-11-04) and :latest
'     2.1.325 declare no volume@1 and no host-mount@1; neither do sbx/codex
'     and sbx/opencode. History then lives in the long-lived sandbox itself.
'   sbx/claude-sessions, codex-sessions, cursor-sessions: opt-in mixins. Each
'     declares one host-mount@1 at /home/agent/<agent>-history, and an install
'     hook symlinks the session dirs into it. 1.0.0 shared one dir across
'     sandboxes. 1.1.0 (Hub tag 2026-11-13) links into
'     claude-history/<sandbox name>: "Each sandbox uses a subdirectory named
'     after that sandbox, so simultaneous sandboxes do not share one writable
'     session store." https://hub.docker.com/r/sbx/claude-sessions
'   https://github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec/commit/f168691c (2026-11-02):
'     "Add the same opt-in host storage for Claude and remove its private
'     session volumes". It also deleted a postCreate hook that ran `sbx mount`
'     for a live bind. Neither is a per-file copy: proveo's copy has no
'     upstream counterpart. [Inference] Tying that examples/ commit to the
'     published kit is inference.
' RELEASES (https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/releases):
'   v0.42.0 (2026-09-07): a new sandbox reusing a deleted name "no longer
'     inherits its … agent session history."
'   v0.50.0 (2026-10-26) reversed it: "Persistent kit volumes retain data
'     across kit updates and sandbox removal and recreation with the same
'     name."
'   v0.51.0 (2026-11-03): "Built-in agent names now resolve to published kits
'     at `docker.io/sbx/<name>:latest`"; "Additional workspaces accept
'     `PATH:TARGET[:ro]`".
'   v0.53.0 (2026-11-11): "`sbx df` reports … managed-volume disk usage".
' OPEN UPSTREAM:
'   https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/issues/842 "No supported way to
'     delete local persistent kit volumes (volume commands are cloud-only)".
'   sbx#775 "Locks don't cross VMs": several sandboxes writing one
'     host-mount@1 file lost 93–97% of their writes.
'   https://github.com/docker/sandbox-kit-spec/issues/171 asks to define
'     host-mount locking limits and read-only access.
' SPEC VS CLI: the volume@1 spec at main says kit references "do not determine
'   volume identity"; v0.50.0's `sbx rm --help` still says the same name "with
'   the same kit" reattaches. [Inference] A conforming sbx would reattach by
'   name alone.
'
' ── THE LEAK S3 STOPS (measured 2026-11-14, read-only) ─────────────────────
' The vendored claude kit declares the five volume@1 of sbx/claude 2.1.267
' (internal/sbx/third_party/claude.yaml). proveo writes each run's kit to a
' new directory (sandbox.go: KitDir under RunDir), so the kit source changes
' every run and sbx v0.50 reattaches none of them. The sbx datastore held
' 1,710 records labelled persistent-volume: 1,360 from per-run kit dirs, 350
' from test and probe temp dirs. One stable name held 75 volumes across 15 kit
' identities, five per create. Each fresh projects volume also received the
' whole host store (1.3 GB) until the stopgap scoped the restore (F7).
'
' ── THE TWO EXCEPTIONS TO STANDARDIZE (S1) ─────────────────────────────────
' EXCEPTION 1, OpenCode's retained engine (engine-local-history.puml).
'   What it is: normalEndOf returns endRetainEngine for an OpenCode target, so
'   a clean end keeps the named sandbox. The next run re-attaches, and OpenCode
'   opens its own SQLite on the engine's disk. A replacement (image, kit or
'   mount change) exports the database over `sbx exec` stdout to
'   opencode/carry/<engine>.db, and a new engine imports it once over `sbx
'   exec -i`.
'   What it teaches:
'     * It is sbx's model already: continuity with no copy on the common path.
'     * SQLite stays on the VM's own disk. WAL coordinates writers through
'       -shm, which works only within one host. [Unverified] A database shared
'       across VMs through a mount was never measured; sbx#775 says locks do
'       not cross VMs.
'     * A replacement still needs a carry, and the carry needs a
'       commit-or-nothing protocol (its D5: a failed import removes the fresh
'       engine and keeps the source).
'     * `sbx rm`, the Ctrl+C remove and name reuse lose the history unless a
'       carry ran first. Engines in different workspaces diverge from one
'       share snapshot, and nothing merges them.
' EXCEPTION 2, hermes's live bind (hermes-persistence.puml).
'   What it is: agent_home.go puts HERMES_HOME=<state home>/hermes/data in the
'   workload env. That is the host path of the proveo-home bind every VM
'   already gets (sandbox.go Home, PROVEO_STATE_HOME). No copy runs; the agent,
'   `sbx exec` and SSH sessions all write the host directly.
'   What it teaches:
'     * A live host directory needs no new sbx capability on v0.50.0: the bind
'       exists in every VM (P2, way a).
'     * Everything survives `sbx rm`, even a sandbox that never tore down
'       cleanly. Nothing waits at teardown.
'     * It is one directory for every workspace (920M, 247k files), so two
'       hermes sandboxes share one state.db. [Unverified] SQLite over the bind
'       across VMs was never measured; sbx#775 measured lost writes for the
'       class.
'     * A live bind inherits the bind's failure modes: a host-side inode
'       replacement cuts the guest's view
'       (_spec/internal/sbx/virtiofs-cwd-invalidation.puml).
' THE RULE THEY SUGGEST. [Inference] Keep the sandbox (exception 1's half).
' Put append-only history on a live host dir (exception 2's half). Keep a
' SQLite store on the VM's disk and carry it only at a replacement, as OpenCode
' does, until sbx#775 or kit-spec#171 says a cross-VM writer is safe (Q3).
'
' ── P0 THE STOPGAP (this branch; built, uncommitted) ───────────────────────
' Built; state-sync.puml carries the detail and every pin:
'   F2  A failed save keeps the sandbox: normalEndOf → endKeepUnsaved, retire
'       keeps it too, and the Ctrl+C forced remove still removes.
'   F3  No destination name is written in place (stage + rename, temp +
'       rename). A clean restore writes PROVEO_STATE_RESTORED in /dev/shm;
'       save waits up to 60s for it, then refuses.
'   F4  _proveo_state_plan copies by direction, newer wins; a 5s same-tick
'       window applies to save only.
'   F5  The restore of projects/ copies only this run's keys: the workdir, its
'       physical path, every `git worktree list` path, the git common root.
'   F6  `proveo rm <kept>` saves first (GuardedSaveStateArgs; exit 3 skips an
'       image older than the guard).
'   D1  Teardown and retire skip the save only when sbx.Gone proves the
'       sandbox gone.
'   D2  SaveStateArgs fails when the config save or the state save fails.
'   D3  Every kept or not-removed fix line names `sbx rm --force <name>`; a
'       directory past the exec argument limit lands through `xargs -0`.
'   D4  Retire has its own fix line. D5: sibling worktrees are restored. D7:
'       clock skew is an accepted limit. D8: neutral homes, pinned by
'       TestNoTrackedFileNamesARealHome.
' Built in pass 2 (S2, S3), uncommitted beside the rest of P0:
'   * internal/sbx/third_party/claude.yaml declares no volume@1, as upstream
'     after 2.1.267; TestNoVendoredKitDeclaresAVolume pins every vendored kit.
'   * The manifest names the copied dirs: state: [projects, todos] on the
'     .claude mount, sent as PROVEO_STATE_DIRS (proveohome.StateSet).
'     proveo_sync_state carries those, projects/ scoped to this run's keys,
'     and _proveo_config_skips keeps the config sync off them.
'   * An env with no PROVEO_STATE_DIRS (a sandbox an older CLI created on this
'     image) falls back to the volume dirs /proc/mounts lists, minus
'     sessions, statsig and shell-snapshots, and the config sync prunes
'     every volume (state-sync.puml, row C).
'   * S2: sessions/, statsig/, shell-snapshots/, daemon.lock,
'     daemon.status.json, daemon.log, daemon/ and jobs/ stay VM-local through
'     transient: in defs/claudecode/harness.manifest, never deny: deny runs
'     scrubDeny (proveohome.go, os.RemoveAll), which would delete
'     ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions, against S3.
'   * Sandboxes an older image created still hold volumes, and the state
'     clause of SaveStateArgs stays: a retire saves them; `proveo rm` skips
'     their save (D6, exit 3) and removes them.
'   * Not touched: the 1,710 stranded records and ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions
'     (78 records, one torn mid-write), for the owner.
' WHY sessions/ NEVER CROSSES (the sessions study, Claude Code 2.1.323):
'   sessions/<pid>.json registers a live process for concurrent-session and
'   crash detection; /resume and `claude -c` read projects/
'   (https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-directory). Inside a VM no record
'   is ever swept, because IS_SANDBOX turns the sweep off. Every VM boots with
'   the same pidDomain, so a carried record from a dead VM can count as live:
'   `claude -c` then skips a transcript or stops ("registered from another
'   machine or container"), and the concurrent-session tip miscounts.
'   daemon.lock carries no pidDomain.
'
' ── P1 KEEP THE NAMED SANDBOX, FOR EVERY HARNESS ───────────────────────────
' 1. A stable kit source per (harness, workspace). Today KitDir is
'    <RunDir>/sbx/kit (sandbox.go), new every run. Move it to one dir per
'    sandbox name under the proveo state dir, rewritten in place. sbx then
'    finds any kit storage again by the identity it keys on: a volume@1
'    reattach, the host-mount@1 key of P2 way c, package-caches.puml's cache
'    mount. [Unverified] Whether sbx keys a local kit on the dir path or on its
'    content (sync check R11). The receipt already ignores the kit dir path,
'    so moving it marks no sandbox stale (kit-lifecycle.puml).
' 2. Keep on a clean end. normalEndOf's retainsEngine becomes true for every
'    harness: endRetainEngine generalises to one endRetain, whose closing line
'    names the re-attach. Forced, stranded and unsaved keep their precedence
'    above it. The OpenCode branch stops being a case. [Inference] sbx stops a
'    local sandbox about 30 s after its last session disconnects
'    (engine-local-history.puml, REHOMED), so a kept sandbox costs disk, not
'    memory.
' 3. Retire still carries state. A kit, image, mount or env change still
'    retires the sandbox: receipt mismatch → carry the clone home → `sbx rm`
'    → create the same name. Until P2, retire runs the stopgap's save; after
'    P2 the history is already on the host, and retire carries the clone only.
'    [Inference] Every `mise run build <harness>` changes the image, so most
'    retires follow a rebuild; one name already showed 11 kit identities.
' 4. The reboot restore is safe now. The revision rated "retain everything"
'    as F4 on every run. P0's newer-wins restore keeps a newer guest turn, so a
'    re-attach that boots a stopped VM reverts nothing, barring clock skew
'    (D7) and pre-P0 images.
' P1 alone keeps history between runs; P2 keeps it across a retire and `sbx
' rm`, and makes it readable on the host.
' Tests: the normalEndOf table (every harness keeps), a teardown report that
' keeps on success, and an e2e that runs twice and re-attaches by name.
'
' ── P2 HISTORY ON A LIVE HOST DIRECTORY PER (harness, workspace) ───────────
' Layout, after claude-sessions 1.1.0 (per name, never one shared dir):
'   ~/.proveo/history/<harness>/<sandbox name>/{projects,todos,…}
'   The sandbox name already encodes (target, workspace):
'   proveo-<target>-<sha256(workspace)[:4]> (sbx.SandboxName). A worktree
'   clone keys on its repository root (sandboxKey), so sibling worktrees share
'   one dir, which `claude --resume` across worktrees (D5) needs.
'   Unlike the mixin, sessions/ is never linked (S2).
'   [Inference] A 4-byte hash collides rarely; a marker file holding the
'   workspace path would detect it.
' Three ways to put that dir in the VM, cheapest first:
'   a. The existing ~/.proveo bind. Every VM already mounts the proveo home at
'      its host path and exports PROVEO_STATE_HOME; hermes runs on it today.
'      The seed symlinks ~/.claude/projects and todos into it, as the mixin's
'      install hook does. Works on v0.50.0. [Inference] Every VM can read
'      every workspace's history, as today.
'   b. v0.51 additional workspaces, PATH:TARGET[:ro]: the per-name dir mounted
'      at its target with no symlink, and the VM sees only its own workspace.
'      Needs sbx v0.51.0 or later (Q5). [Unverified] That a TARGET may sit
'      under the agent's HOME.
'   c. host-mount@1 in proveo's kit plus `sbx create --mount HOST:PATH`,
'      upstream's exact shape. Needs P1's stable kit source or `--mount` on
'      every create. Without either, each run gets a new runtime-owned host dir
'      that `sbx rm` keeps: the leak S3 stops, in a new place (intent check C3).
' Delete with it: proveo_sync_state, _proveo_state_entries,
' _proveo_volume_dirs, _proveo_state_tree, _proveo_state_plan,
' _proveo_state_place, _proveo_await_restore with the restore marker
' (PROVEO_STATE_RESTORED), the seed's restore call, the state clause of
' _proveo_config_skips, the manifest's state: field (HomeMount.State,
' ValidState), proveohome.StateSet with PROVEO_STATE_DIRS, and the state
' clause of SaveStateArgs. Once the migration below has run, the key
' functions go too: _proveo_claude_project_key, _proveo_claude_project_roots
' and _proveo_claude_project_dirs. The SaveStateArgs clause stays one release
' behind `declare -F proveo_sync_state`, for sandboxes older images created
' (sync check R4).
' The clock-skew limit (D7) and F3's truncation class leave with the copy.
' Migration: the first run per name copies this workspace's keys from
' ~/.proveo/.claude/projects into the per-name dir; the stopgap's key function
' names them. The old tree stays read-only, for the owner to remove.
' codex and cursor: their history travels by config sync today (codex
' sessions/**.jsonl, history.jsonl, state_5.sqlite with -wal and -shm; cursor
' chats/ and projects/). Upstream ships codex-sessions and cursor-sessions
' mixins of the claude shape. The jsonl dirs move to the per-name dir;
' state_5.sqlite follows OpenCode's rule (on the VM's disk, carried at a
' retire) until Q3 is answered. [Unverified] Cursor's on-disk chat format.
' Harness-wide files (claude's and codex's history.jsonl, settings) stay on
' config sync: they are not per workspace, and F8–F11 still apply to them.
' Tests: TestNoVendoredKitDeclaresAVolume stays; a contract test that the
' seed links projects/ and todos/ to the per-name dir. e2e: `claude -c`
' resumes across two runs; two concurrent workspaces keep their turns; a
' retire keeps the history with no save.
'
' ── P3 REFRESH THE CLONE ON RE-ATTACH ──────────────────────────────────────
' sbx fixes clone mode at create, so a re-attached sandbox keeps the clone of
' the run that created it. When the host's HEAD has moved since:
'   never refresh   the agent works on a silent fork of an old base, and the
'                   operator reconciles it on the host
'   reset to HEAD   discards the clone's uncommitted work and moves the agent
'                   off its own branch
' Proposed. Teardown already commits a snapshot of uncommitted work and lifts
' the clone's commits to refs/proveo/<sid>/* (clone-workspace.puml), so at a
' re-attach the clone's work is already mirrored on the host. Then:
'   1. Fetch the host's refs into the clone from /run/sandbox/source, which
'      the git docs call "available at `/run/sandbox/source`, but only with
'      read access". [Inference] That mount is live, so it shows today's refs.
'   2. Fast-forward the base branch only when the clone's tree is clean and
'      the fast-forward is clean. Never rewrite the agent's own branch.
'   3. Say what moved, e.g. "host main moved N commits; <branch> is based on
'      the old main", and leave the rebase to the agent or the operator.
' The agent's own branch stays checked out across runs, so the operator sees
' one branch growing, not N ref namespaces.
' reusable-clone.puml lists the touch points (decideClone, CloneFetchArgs,
' PreserveClone, liftClonedOutput) and its measure-first rule.
' [Inference] Direct mode (--clone=false) has no clone and nothing to refresh:
' the guest reads the host tree live.
'
' ── P4 RETIRE THE SPECIAL CASES ────────────────────────────────────────────
' OpenCode: P1 makes its retention the rule, so endRetainEngine and the
' OpenCode-only branch go. Its carry stays the one SQLite carry until Q3
' answers whether a cross-VM SQLite writer is safe. Then either:
'   * the carry generalises to every SQLite store at a retire (codex
'     state_5.sqlite, hermes state.db), or
'   * the database moves to the per-name host dir and the carry is deleted.
' hermes: HERMES_HOME is one dir for every workspace, the opposite of S1's
' per-(harness, workspace) rule. Options for the owner:
'   * per name: HERMES_HOME=<history>/hermes/<sandbox name>; memories, skills
'     and the vault stop crossing workspaces unless they are split out;
'   * shared, one writer: keep one dir and refuse a second live hermes
'     sandbox, with a host-side lock, since guest locks do not cross VMs;
'   * shared as today, with sbx#775's lost-write risk recorded.
' [Inference] Hermes is a personal agent whose memory is meant to cross
' workspaces, so the per-name split costs it the most.
'
' ── OPEN QUESTIONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Q1 TWO RUNS ON ONE WORKSPACE. One name per (harness, workspace), so a second
'    run re-attaches to the first's live sandbox. The launch path has no
'    liveness guard and no run lock (sync check). [Unverified] Today the
'    first teardown may remove the VM the second still uses (F13). sbx's
'    pattern is parallel sessions in one sandbox (the git and claude-code
'    docs, sbx#775). P1 removes the `sbx rm` on a clean end. Still open: a
'    teardown must not stop or retire a sandbox another session holds. S2
'    makes sessions/ VM-local, which is what parallel sessions in one VM need.
' Q2 proveo clean AND DISK. Kept sandboxes accumulate, one per (harness,
'    workspace), and `proveo clean` lists none of them. `proveo clean
'    --homes` removes ~/.proveo without checking for running sandboxes (F15);
'    after P2 that deletes live history. v0.53.0's `sbx df` reports
'    managed-volume use. A host ENOSPC flips kept guests read-only, with no
'    in-place fix.
' Q3 LOCKS ACROSS VMs (sbx#775, kit-spec#171). Neither flock nor fcntl crosses
'    VMs. Exposed: hermes's state.db over the bind; claude's
'    projects/<root key>/memory/*.md when two VMs share a repository; codex's
'    SQLite if it moves out. Per-name dirs (P2) confine sharing to one
'    workspace, and Q1's one-sandbox answer confines it to one VM.
' Q4 CLOCK SKEW. P0's newer-wins trusts the VM and host clocks (D7). P1 makes
'    restores rare, and P2 deletes them. [Inference] The VM clock follows the
'    host's, so skew needs a host clock step.
' Q5 THE sbx VERSION FLOOR. The host runs v0.50.0. v0.53.0 (2026-11-11) is the
'    latest release, and v0.54.0-rc7 (2026-11-13) is out. P2 way b needs
'    v0.51.0, which also resolves built-in agent names to published kits.
'    proveo names no minimum sbx version today.
' Q6 THE STRANDED VOLUMES. 1,710 records wait for sbx#842: v0.50.0 has no
'    local `sbx volume rm`, and `sbx reset` deletes everything. S3 leaves them,
'    and ~/.proveo/.claude/sessions, for the owner. [Inference] A sbx that
'    follows the volume@1 spec at main would reattach them by name, sessions
'    volume included; P0's drop of volume@1 keeps new sandboxes out of that.
title PLANNED — session continuity the sbx way: one kept sandbox\nper (harness, workspace), its history live on the host

actor "operator" as OP

node "host: proveo run <harness>\nin one workspace" as PV <<host>>
component "host: stable kit source\none dir per sandbox name (P1)" as KIT <<app>>
database "host: <home>/.proveo/history/\n<harness>/<sandbox name>/\nprojects/ · todos/ · jsonl (P2)" as HIST <<db>>
database "host: refs/proveo/<sid>/*\nthe clone's work, lifted each run" as REFS <<db>>

component "sandbox proveo-<harness>-<workspace hash>\nkept between runs (P1)\nagent: claude · codex · cursor · opencode · hermes" as AG <<app>>
database "sandbox: the clone\nfixed at create\nrefreshed on re-attach (P3)" as CLONE <<db>>
database "sandbox: VM-local only (S2)\nsessions/ · daemon.lock\ndaemon/ · jobs/\nSQLite until Q3" as LOCAL <<db>>

component "retire on a kit, image\nor mount change:\nthe same name anew" as RETIRE <<async>>
component "exception 1\nOpenCode retained engine" as OCE <<app>>
component "exception 2\nhermes live HERMES_HOME bind" as HB <<app>>
component "deleted: per-file state sync,\nvendored volume@1,\nretained-engine case" as GONE <<error>>
component "1,710 stranded volume@1\nrecords, waiting for sbx#842" as STRAND <<error>>

OP ARROW_MAIN PV
PV ARROW_MAIN AG : sbx run --name (re-attach)
PV ARROW_OPTIONAL KIT : sbx create only
AG ARROW_MAIN HIST : live dir
AG ARROW_MAIN LOCAL : never carried
CLONE ARROW_QUEUE REFS : teardown lift
REFS ARROW_OPTIONAL CLONE : re-attach refresh
PV ARROW_OPTIONAL RETIRE : receipt changed
RETIRE ARROW_MAIN CLONE : same name, new clone
OCE ARROW_OPTIONAL AG : retention becomes the rule
HB ARROW_OPTIONAL HIST : the live dir becomes the rule
GONE ARROW_ERROR STRAND : P0 stops the growth

note right of AG
  **One sandbox per (harness, workspace).** A
  clean end keeps it, and the next run
  re-attaches by name, as OpenCode's engine
  does today.
end note

note bottom of HIST
  **History lives on the host, per name.** The
  agent writes it live, so a retire or sbx rm
  loses nothing and no teardown copy runs.
end note

note bottom of LOCAL
  **VM-local, never carried (S2).** sessions/
  registers live PIDs, and every VM boots with
  the same pidDomain, so a carried record lies.
end note

note left of CLONE
  **The clone outlives the run (P3).** Re-attach
  fetches the host's refs, fast-forwards a clean
  base and never rewrites the agent's branch.
end note

note bottom of RETIRE
  **A changed kit or image still retires.** The
  same name is created anew. After P2 only the
  clone is carried: the history is on the host.
end note

note bottom of OCE
  **Exception 1 teaches retention.** SQLite
  stays on the VM's disk and crosses only at a
  replacement, through a commit-or-nothing carry.
end note

note bottom of HB
  **Exception 2 teaches the live dir.** No copy
  and no new sbx capability, but one HERMES_HOME
  for every workspace, shared across VMs.
end note

note bottom of GONE
  **Deleted in P2 and P4.** The per-file state
  sync, the vendored volume@1 and the retained-
  engine case go. Config sync stays.
end note

note bottom of STRAND
  **Left for the owner (S3).** No local command
  removes a kept kit volume on v0.50.0, so the
  records wait for sbx#842.
end note

note left of KIT
  **A stable kit source (P1).** One dir per
  sandbox name, so sbx finds kit storage again
  by the identity it keys on.
end note

legend bottom
  **Phases** — S1–S3 decided by the owner, 2026-11-14
  ==
  **P0 stopgap** (built, uncommitted): no failed save removes a sandbox; newer-wins, staged copies;
  projects/ scoped to this workspace's keys; ""proveo rm"" saves first; no vendored ""volume@1"";
  the manifest names the copied dirs; sessions/ and the daemon files stay VM-local.
  --
  **P1 keep**: a stable kit source per name; every harness keeps its sandbox on a clean end; retire
  on a kit or image change still carries state.
  --
  **P2 live history**: a per-name host dir (the proveo-home bind, v0.51 ""PATH:TARGET"", or
  ""host-mount@1"" + ""--mount""); delete ""proveo_sync_state"" and its helpers.
  --
  **P3 refresh**: fetch host refs on re-attach, fast-forward a clean base, keep the agent's branch.
  --
  **P4 standardize**: OpenCode's retention is the rule; its carry and hermes's shared home await Q3.
  ==
  **Open**: Q1 two runs, one workspace · Q2 clean and disk · Q3 locks across VMs · Q4 clock skew ·
  Q5 sbx version floor · Q6 stranded volumes
end legend
@enduml
